rols), and PCI DSS (payment-card industry compliance) certifications. These are critical differentiators for buyers in regulated industries (finance, healthcare, public sector) where the provider's compliance posture directly affects the buyer's own audit trail. The certifications cover all six datacenter regions."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Does Cherry Servers offer bare-metal servers?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Yes. Cherry Servers started as a bare-metal operator in 2000 and still sells dedicated servers alongside the Cloud VPS product line. Bare-metal tiers include AMD EPYC 7402P (24c/48t, $49/mo entry) and Intel Xeon Scalable options with full root access, hardware-level control, and 10 Gbps unmetered uplinks on dedicated configurations. The dual cloud + bare-metal product line is rare among SMB-tier European providers."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "How does Cherry Servers compare to RackNerd?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Cherry Servers and RackNerd occupy different positions in the 2026 VPS market. RackNerd targets absolute lowest price ($1.99-$10.98/yr promotional) with US-centric datacenter locations and is ideal for personal projects, VPN endpoints, and developer test environments. Cherry Servers targets the regulated SMB market with 6 regions (4 EU + US + Singapore), ISO 27001 / SOC 2 / PCI DSS certifications, and dual cloud + bare-metal product lines from $3.51/mo entry. RackNerd has no EU jurisdiction or compliance certifications; Cherry Servers has no $1.99/mo tier. They are complementary, not directly substitutable."}}]}
